# One `Shared` per process: defines `process_regions`.
axiom_process_shared	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# A field fixed once its permission is frozen: no vstd counterpart.
axiom_shared_regions	raw pointer (internal)	none (assumption)
axiom_shared_meta	raw pointer (internal)	none (assumption)
axiom_shared_built	raw pointer (internal)	none (assumption)
# The caller's storage (`init`'s safety contract), once per process.
Shared::begin	raw pointer from C caller	none (assumption)
# An FFI call that may re-enter the allocator: the nested entries leave
# the token as they found it (the slot premise).
pthread_setspecific	FFI/syscall	none (assumption)
# Empty-template register hint: verus/emptyasm/run.sh checks the block adds
# no instruction to the shipped code (a verus/emptyasm/blocks.txt row);
# Kani checks the load, on a copy whose lines seams.sh --check requires
# to equal the body's but for the rows verus/kani/pins.txt marks `-only`.
ClassLine::guard_word	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Kani: heap::shared::kani_guard_word::guard_word_is_the_three_fields, const assert: `ClassLine::guard_word`'s word in src/heap/shared.rs, and emptyasm: guard_word in src/heap/shared.rs; not checked: the body itself, since the harness runs a copy of its load without the asm! block (Kani has no model of inline assembly), whose lines `sh verus/seams.sh --check` requires to equal the body's but for the rows verus/kani/pins.txt marks `-only`, today the opening brace and the asm! block, with comment and blank lines not compared)
